Z||000005||Dave Gunsul||06-10-2001||06:17 PM||||The wheels look okay but how heavy are they?<BR>A lot of those trick aftermarket wheels are pretty heavy and will slow you down.<P>Yes i'm addicted to acceleration, how did you know?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000006||Loki||06-10-2001||06:33 PM||||Hey Smooooooooooth, whats up? Im so glad to be back in texas.....Hate the weather but, cant have it all..As for weight...There not as heavy as alot of wheels..Most good wheel companies  wheels are light enough to not really matter.......I would think there close if not lighter than the factory turbo fin rims<P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998||||reg||1
Z||000007||Dave Gunsul||06-10-2001||07:14 PM||||Actually a lot of the aftermarket wheels are quite heavy. Some are pushing 30 IB's!<BR>The 15 inch GT stock wheels weigh in around 18 IB's and the 14 inchers are probably around 12-15.<BR>I just put light-weight racing wheels on my GT and they do make a difference, not huge, but a difference none the less.<P>------------------<BR>Dave Gunsul<BR>N.I.F.E. member<BR>86 GT modified<BR>85 SE daily driver||||reg||1
Z||000008||AusFiero||06-11-2001||09:08 AM||||For some high quality light rims cheap has anyone tried Subaru WRX wheels? Bolt pattern is right, not sure on the offset. Wish I knew that when I had my WRX, I woulda tried them on.<P>The alloy used in Subaru rims is very high quality. Up there with Porsche and Ferrari. Weight wise they are very light. Dunno the exact weight but I have changed one and though at the time, god this weighs nothing.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/fiero5.gif">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A><BR>Need a Subwoofer Console or Speaker Door Pods?||||reg||1
